<title>FRANCE: EIFB positive on Axa-UAP merger.</title>
<headline>EIFB positive on Axa-UAP merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Axa-UAP is the French insurance group offering the best outlook in terms of earnings growth, said brokerage EIFB in a study of the two companies' planned merger.</p>
<p>EIFB said it had a price target of 384 francs for the new merged entity on a 12 to 18 month horizon.</p>
<p>&quot;In operating terms, the group presents good fundamentals at the same time as being less sensitive to the cyclical nature of the insurance business,&quot; EIFB analyst Sami Gotrane said.</p>
<p>Axa was trading at 310.50 francs, down 1.08 percent at 1521 GMT.</p>
<p>Axa and UAP announced last month plans to merge. The new group will be the second largest insurer in the world.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
